      "text": [
        " «إِنْ كَانَ فِي شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ فَلْيُفْطِرْ» فَسُئِلَ أَيُّهُمَا أَفْضَلُ يُقِيمُ وَ يَصُومُ أَوْ يُشَيِّعُهُ قَالَ «يُشَيِّعُهُ إِنَّ اَللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ وَضَعَ اَلصَّوْمَ عَنْهُ إِذَا شَيَّعَهُ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1971 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) was asked about a man who sets out to accompany his brother on a journey for two or three days.\nImam (as) said: \"If it is during the Month of Ramadan, let him break his fast.\"\nHe was then asked: \"Which is better, for him to stay and fast or to accompany his brother?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"To accompany him, for Allah (swt), the Almighty, has exempted him from fasting when he accompanies his brother.\""
        ]
      }
